From 0f2676a37379352b20bb9724c0dc63d9b6d65ddb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Trotter <james@jamesat.dev>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:10:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] api: channel guard: join error text, oper JOIN and removing
 members (channel_access)

POST /v1/channel_access takes joinError (the 473/477 text for clients
+i or +R keeps out), operJoin (opers with the sajoin capability may JOIN
despite +i/+R) and kick/kickReason (remove, as ChanServ, every member
who couldn't join now; the founder, AMODE entries, +I matches and guard
opers stay). Lets an external role system restrict channels to roles
with a clear refusal and take access away from people already inside.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
